CC BY-SA 3.0 is **required**, not merely chosen. `lean/Trans/Recal.lean` is a port
of `common.js` from Naruyoko's `pss-vs-buchholz`, which is licensed CC BY-SA 3.0
(see the External sources section below). A port is a derivative work, so the
ShareAlike condition applies to this repository. It also happens to match the
license of the Googology Wiki (Fandom), where the external analyses this project
checks itself against are published, so material can flow in both directions
without a license mismatch.

**Attribution.** If you reuse this work, credit
"koteitan, bms-rathjen (<https://github.com/koteitan/bms-rathjen>)"
and indicate whether you changed anything. If what you reuse includes
`lean/Trans/Recal.lean` or anything derived from it, credit Naruyoko as well.

**Note for reusers of the Lean sources.** CC BY-SA is a content license, not a
software license: it has no source-provision clause, no patent grant, and is not
compatible with the GNU GPL or most other software copyleft. This is a real cost
and it cannot simply be undone — `lean/Trans/Recal.lean` carries ShareAlike from
upstream, so relicensing it is not the maintainer's to grant. The rest of `lean/`
is this project's own work; if you need it under different terms, open an issue.

